<Input><Text-field style="Text" bold="true" layout="Normal" alignment="centred"><Font bold="true">MATH 4503/6503 worksheet 4: Euler and trapezoidal stencils to solve </Font><Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation><Font bold="false">

Irfan Javed
<Font italic="true">January 28, 2026</Font></Font></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" bold="true" layout="Normal" alignment="centred"></Text-field><Text-field style="Normal" layout="Normal">The purpose of this worksheet is to derive the three simplest numerical stencils to solve the first order equation<Equation executable="false" style="Normal" input-equation="" display=""></Equation> and study some of their properties. We first write down the ODE using the D notation:</Text-field>
</Input>
