<Group labelreference="L856" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">We see that the one-step error for the forward and backward schemes is <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation>. Futhermore, the leading order terms for these stencils are negatives of each other. Since the trapezoidal scheme is the average of the forward and backward algorithms, this explains why the leading order error for the trapeziodal scheme is <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation>. In other words, the trapezoidal scheme is more accurate than the other two. Note that if all we are after are the leading order terms in the errors, we can just expand the above in a low order series.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L831" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">for j from 1 to 3 do:
    Error[Labels[j]] := series(Error[Labels[j]], h, 0);
od;</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+JkkmRXJyb3JHRig2I1EuRm9yd2FyZH5FdWxlckYoKyVJImhHRigtSSJPR0YlNiMiIiIiIiM3I0Yx</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+JkkmRXJyb3JHRig2I1EvQmFja3dhcmR+RXVsZXJGKCslSSJoR0YoLUkiT0dGJTYjIiIiIiIjNyNGMQ==</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+JkkmRXJyb3JHRig2I1EsVHJhcGV6b2lkYWxGKCslSSJoR0YoLUkiT0dGJTYjIiIiIiIkNyNGMQ==</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L829" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">We now turn our attention to actual numerical algorithms employing these stencils. Since the forward Euler scheme is explicit, it is particularly easy to develop some code for it that works for an arbitrary function <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUkjbWlHRiQ2JlEiZkYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUrZXhlY3V0YWJsZUdRJmZhbHNlRicvJSxtYXRodmFyaWFudEdRJ2l0YWxpY0YnRjIvRjZRJ25vcm1hbEYn">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUkjbWlHRiQ2JlEiZkYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUrZXhlY3V0YWJsZUdRJmZhbHNlRicvJSxtYXRodmFyaWFudEdRJ2l0YWxpY0YnRjIvRjZRJ25vcm1hbEYn</Equation>. It is useful to rewrite the stencil with <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation> isolated on the left-hand side.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L830" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">eq20 := isolate(Stencils[1], y[i+1]);</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+SSVlcTIwR0YoLyZJInlHRig2IywmSSJpR0YoIiIiRjRGNCwmJkYwNiNGM0Y0KiYtSSJmR0YoNiQmSSJ4R0YoRjdGNkY0SSJoR0YoRjRGNDcjRi4=</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L838" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">Now, we can transcribe this as a mapping that takes the stepsize and the old values <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYmLUklbXN1YkdGJDYlLUkjbWlHRiQ2JlEieUYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUrZXhlY3V0YWJsZUdRJmZhbHNlRicvJSxtYXRodmFyaWFudEdRJ2l0YWxpY0YnLUYjNiYtRi82JlEiaUYnRjJGNUY4RjJGNUY4LyUvc3Vic2NyaXB0c2hpZnRHUSIwRictRi82I1EhRidGNS9GOVEnbm9ybWFsRic=">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYmLUklbXN1YkdGJDYlLUkjbWlHRiQ2JlEieUYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUrZXhlY3V0YWJsZUdRJmZhbHNlRicvJSxtYXRodmFyaWFudEdRJ2l0YWxpY0YnLUYjNiYtRi82JlEiaUYnRjJGNUY4RjJGNUY4LyUvc3Vic2NyaXB0c2hpZnRHUSIwRictRi82I1EhRidGNS9GOVEnbm9ybWFsRic=</Equation> and <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUklbXN1YkdGJDYlLUkjbWlHRiQ2JlEieEYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUrZXhlY3V0YWJsZUdRJmZhbHNlRicvJSxtYXRodmFyaWFudEdRJ2l0YWxpY0YnLUYjNiYtRi82JlEiaUYnRjJGNUY4RjJGNUY4LyUvc3Vic2NyaXB0c2hpZnRHUSIwRidGNS9GOVEnbm9ybWFsRic=">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUklbXN1YkdGJDYlLUkjbWlHRiQ2JlEieEYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUrZXhlY3V0YWJsZUdRJmZhbHNlRicvJSxtYXRodmFyaWFudEdRJ2l0YWxpY0YnLUYjNiYtRi82JlEiaUYnRjJGNUY4RjJGNUY4LyUvc3Vic2NyaXB0c2hpZnRHUSIwRidGNS9GOVEnbm9ybWFsRic=</Equation> and returns the new value <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation>.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L840" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">y_new := (h, x_old, y_old) -&gt; y_old+f(x_old, y_old)*h;</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+SSZ5X25ld0dGKGYqNiVJImhHRihJJnhfb2xkR0YoSSZ5X29sZEdGKEYoNiRJKW9wZXJhdG9yR0YoSSZhcnJvd0dGKEYoLCY5JiIiIiomLUkiZkdGKDYkOSVGN0Y4OSRGOEY4RihGKEYoNyNGLg==</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L833" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">We could have equivalently accomplished this by using the <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">unapply</Font> command, which converts expressions into mappings without our having to rewrite them manually:</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L836" drawlabel="true">
